# The preview build renders records that are held from publication, which
# today means findings whose subjects have not yet been given their seven
# days. Committing it would put them in a repository that may be pushed,
# which is the thing the hold exists to prevent.
#
# It used to be written to brand/, and that was the same mistake one more
# time. brand/ is the directory whose whole purpose is to be published, and
# the preview was found sitting in it being served on every interface by a
# throwaway http.server left running after an afternoon of looking at the
# page. Every other layer had been fixed by then. Not tracking a file does
# nothing about a file being read. It now goes to private/, which is not a
# publish root and exists for exactly one reason: nothing in it should ever
# leave this machine.
brand/register.preview.html
private/

# That reasoning was right and was applied to the rendered page while the
# records themselves stayed committed, in plain text, verdict field and all.
# The gate held the derived artifact and left the source in the open, so the
# first push would have published every finding the hold exists to withhold.
#
# Held records now live here and are not tracked. What is tracked instead is
# records/held.manifest.json, which commits to each held record by sha256
# without disclosing what it says. That is a stronger guarantee than keeping
# them in git was: when a record publishes, anyone can hash it and see that it
# matches the value committed on the day it was issued, which is what makes
# "the verdict is fixed before the window opens" checkable rather than
# promised. suite/hold.py maintains it and hooks/pre-push enforces it.
records/held/
